{
  "dom_id": "step-q357178",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "The temperature inside a freezer drops by $2.5{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}$ every hour for $4$ hours. What is the total change in temperature after $4$ hours?",
  "worked_solution": "The temperature decreases by $2.5{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}$ each hour.\n\nSince the change is a decrease and occurs for $4$ hours, the total change can be written as repeated subtraction of $2.5:$\n\n$$\n{{-\\,2.5-2.5-2.5-2.5}_{⏟}}_{4\\text{ times}}\n$$\n\nRepeated subtraction can also be written using multiplication:\n\n$$\n4\\times (-2.5)\n$$\n\nEvaluating the product, we get\n\n$$\n4\\times (-2.5)=-10.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total change in temperature after $4$ hours is $-10{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}.$",
